  "description": "DUWLIT crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C38 H66 Gd2 Mn1 N4 O16 3+,3(N1 O3 1-),4(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd1A (Gd) has 4 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 4 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a chain with approximately linear metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 1.073-3.413 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 15.78-107.39°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C38H74N7MnGd2O29. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 3 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
